                    {
                        "sense_id": "e716766a-f3a2-3f97-afb1-0c3965c64228",
                        "entry_id": "00117e6a-6ee1-3bcf-a85d-5d86e60a752a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Covered in trees; Wooded; woodsy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d3ddd4db-0f34-4b6e-a9e7-7a4987564768",
                                "sense_id": "e716766a-f3a2-3f97-afb1-0c3965c64228",
                                "text": "So saying, by the hand he took me raised, And over fields and waters, as in air, Smooth sliding without step, last led me up A woodly mountain; whose high top was plain, A circuit wide enclosed, with goodliest trees Planted, with walks and bowers;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4caf1cb0-5465-41e0-8452-b624699fbce6",
                                "sense_id": "e716766a-f3a2-3f97-afb1-0c3965c64228",
                                "text": "Argonne, a woodly tract in France, partly in Upper Champagne, and partly in the Lower Barrois."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "45afe1ea-9876-4e99-808b-6ed3286eeda3",
                                "sense_id": "e716766a-f3a2-3f97-afb1-0c3965c64228",
                                "text": "SHALEFLEET. The name was probably derived from shaw, a woodly glen, and fleet, a running stream ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "73b2f6f0-1932-448d-9cca-7eb336d027a2",
                                "sense_id": "e716766a-f3a2-3f97-afb1-0c3965c64228",
                                "text": "It were a woodly country and de boy outrun he chasers."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d478494e-3a69-3770-b72a-88627d2bdf4f",
                        "entry_id": "00117e6a-6ee1-3bcf-a85d-5d86e60a752a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having tough, woody stems; woody."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dc5f67a1-af1c-4dc7-8121-103d7bb0c811",
                                "sense_id": "d478494e-3a69-3770-b72a-88627d2bdf4f",
                                "text": "Cuttings of bedding plants may nnow be made freely if wanted for next season, as young cuttings rooted in the fall make soft-wooded plants as pelargoniums, fuchsias, verbenas, heliotropes, &c.' with roses and plants of a woodly nature, however , the old plants usually do best."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b51e2929-49ea-49aa-b46b-53e2175eb8db",
                                "sense_id": "d478494e-3a69-3770-b72a-88627d2bdf4f",
                                "text": "These are Sarracenia rubra which occurs in bogs and savannahs and Schisandra glabra a woodly vine found in rich woods ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "061c9202-54e9-4df7-b4fb-9ff20b883f1e",
                                "sense_id": "d478494e-3a69-3770-b72a-88627d2bdf4f",
                                "text": "In some regions of the African continent and South America, cassava (Manihot esculenta), which is a woodly shrub, is consumed boiled or fermented (Fossi and Ndjouenkeu, 2017)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
